 36MG    9BE(48CA,X):T1/2:XUNDL-2      2023LU07                           202309
 36MG c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2023Lu07:                          
 36MG2c  Phys Rev C 108, 014329 (2023)                                          
 36MG c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), August 08, 2023.                      
 36MG c  2023Lu07: experiments to study decays of {+36}Al and {+36}Mg were      
 36MG2c  carried out at NSCL-MSU, and at FRIB-MSU facilities. At the NSCL-MSU,  
 36MG3c  {+36}Mg activity was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X),E({+48}Ca)=140      
 36MG4c  MeV/nucleon, followed by separation of fragments using A1900 fragment  
 36MG5c  separator. Mixed radioactive beam centered around {+33}Na was          
 36MG6c  delivered to the NSCL |b-decay counting station, where two Si PIN      
 36MG7c  detectors and a scintillator provided the information about the        
 36MG8c  energy loss (|DE) and time-of-flight (tof) for particle identification 
 36MG9c  of the ions. The separated ions were implanted in a CeBr{-3}           
 36MGAc  scintillator detector which was coupled to a position-sensitive        
 36MGBc  photomultiplier tube (PSPMT), and surrounded by the 16 segmented       
 36MGCc  SeGa array of Ge detectors, and 15 LaBr3 detectors. At the FRIB-MSU,   
 36MGDc  {+36}Mg activity was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,x),E({+48}Ca)=172.3    
 36MGEc  MeV/nucleon, followed by separation of fragments using the Advanced    
 36MGFc  Rare Isotope Separator (ARIS) separator. Mixed radioactive beam        
 36MGGc  centered around {+42}Si was delivered to the FRIB Decay Station        
 36MGHc  Initiator (FDSi), where two Si PIN detectors and a fast scintillator   
 36MGIc  provided the information about the energy loss (|DE) and time-of-flight
 36MGJc  (tof) for particle identification of the ions. The separated ions      
 36MGKc  were implanted in a YSO scintillator detector which was flanked by two 
 36MGLc  scintillator veto detectors immediately upstream and downstream,       
 36MGMc  and surrounded by 11 HPGe clover detectors and 15 fast-timing LaBr{-3} 
 36MGNc  detectors on one side and the neutron detector array VANDLE on the     
 36MGOc  other side. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, half-lives of the 
 36MGPc  decays of {+36}Mg g.s., {+36}Al g.s. and a newly-discovered isomer.    
 36MGQc  Theoretical calculations of levels, J|p and configurations of {+36}Al  
 36MGRc  and {+36}Si using FSU shell-model Hamiltonians with the CoSMo code.    
 36MG  L  0            0+               6.8 MS   10                             
